{
  "requirement": "`AgentConfig` and its backend-specific configuration types implement Serde\nserialization and deserialization. An application can embed them in its own\nconfiguration types; serializing and deserializing a supported configuration\npreserves its settings.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Obligations.** The requirement says three things. `AgentConfig` and its backend-specific types implement Serde serialization and deserialization. An application can embed them in its own configuration types. Round-tripping a supported configuration preserves its settings.\n\n**Tests covering them**\n- `crates/trust-but-verify/src/agent/config.rs#mod[tests]/fn[all_backends_preserve_nested_settings_and_credentials]` is the main test. It runs three backend inputs:\n  - Bedrock, with `aws_profile`, `region`, full `credentials` (including `session_token`) and nested `options`.\n  - OpenAI, with `endpoint`, `api_key` and nested `options`.\n  - Ollama, with `api_key_env` and `options`.\n- For each input it deserializes into `AgentConfig`. It asserts that `serde_json::to_value` equals the original JSON. It then round-trips through a JSON string and asserts the copy equals the original config.\n- The `options` inputs cover every `OptionValue` variant:\n  - integer: `maxTokens`\n  - boolean: `enabled`\n  - float: `0.5`\n  - array: `[\"x\",2,0.5]`\n  - map: `nested` and `reasoning`\n  - string: `\"x\"` and `\"high\"`\n- These assertions would catch dropped or altered fields, credentials, or nested options, and a wrong `backend` tag.\n- `mod[tests]/fn[configuration_debug_hides_credentials]` adds direct Serde checks on `SecretString`. A string deserializes to a `SecretString`. A `SecretString` serializes back to the same string, so credentials are not redacted on serialization. The test also checks that an unknown field makes `AgentConfig` deserialization fail.\n\n**Backend-specific types.** `BedrockConfig`, `OpenAiConfig`, `OllamaConfig` and `BedrockCredentials` are nested in `AgentConfig`. Their Serde behavior is therefore exercised through the enum round trip. The standalone Serde derives add no distinct behavior.\n\n**Embedding.** Embedding in an application type needs no logic beyond the derived traits, and the tests exercise those traits. The tests cover no input class that could expose different required behavior.\n\n**Gaps and acknowledgments.** I found no unacknowledged gap. There are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
